# all_src.bindfile - every row of the GENERATED binding table
# (carrier/gen/bind_table.inc, from carrier/gen/gen_bind_table.py) bound to
# its src/icytower form at once, via --bind-file.
#
# Supersedes all35_src.bindfile, which is kept unchanged so the milestone-12
# "all 35 bound at once" result in carrier/NOTES.md stays reproducible
# exactly as it was measured. The five rows below the rule are the ones the
# generated table added after that milestone (carrier/NOTES.md "binding
# table generated"): add_floor was DIFFERing in vivo until divergence 008
# (notes/living_record.md) fixed its rand() binding, which is why this file
# only becomes usable now.
#
# draw_buffer and start_reward (in-vivo verification pass, 2026-09-07):
# build_blockers.json's asset-seam LNK2019 blocker is resolved -
# carrier/build.cmd now compiles both with pf_lib_bindings.h/
# pf_asset_bindings.h force-included in addition to pf_bindings_src.h
# (carrier/gen/scan_src_defs.py --extra-fi, mechanical CALL-syntax scan),
# so both have a real src form linked into carrier.exe and are listed below.
#
# A concurrently-running pass (batch 8) added a further function
# (draw_scroller) to gen/bind_table.inc after this file's original 40+2
# rows were fixed; it is deliberately left OUT of this list (out of this
# pass's own scope - not verified here) rather than guessed into an
# all-bound run this pass did not test.
#
# Order follows bind_table.inc's own row order.
