# --- added by this in-vivo pass (play() -- PROMOTIONS.md batch 12,
# 2026-09-08): the whole game loop, 17420 bytes, the largest single
# function in the image. KNOWN, MEASURED, REPRODUCIBLE DIVERGENCE --
# included here because the task asked for this exact row, NOT because it
# is verified. Two separate findings, one carrier-layer (harmless) and one
# in play()'s own recovered logic (NOT harmless):
#
# 1. Carrier-layer, harmless: --digest-out/--stop-at-tick produce 0
#    records for ANY run with play bound -- det.cpp's tick safepoint
#    (VA_SAFEPOINT=0x4124f4) is a hardware breakpoint anchored INSIDE
#    play()'s own original machine code, which a src-bound entry-patch
#    redirect bypasses entirely (0 safepoints, MEASURED at shutdown).
#    Per-invocation fn sensor (bind.cpp's own synchronous trampoline, not
#    a hardware breakpoint) is unaffected and reports EQUAL (1 invocation)
#    on human_test.txt.
#
# 2. Recovered-source, NOT harmless: with ONLY play=src bound (no other
#    row in this file), human_test.txt's own final outcome is score=662
#    floor=50, not the divergence-009 witness score=2386 floor=100 --
#    MEASURED, reproduced twice. The frame oracle is EQUAL on every common
#    tick T<=235 (all samples caught before the game climbs far) but
#    --print-globals at matched-ish tick counts shows the divergence is
#    already underway by T~750 (ply[player_id]->level 26 vs 13,
#    ->y 232 vs 61.9675 -- the player is climbing at roughly HALF the
#    rate). All of recording/fast_forward/fast_fast_forward/
#    someCounter__play read IDENTICAL at shutdown in both forms, and the
#    compile is clean (0 errors, the same 5 documented -Wformat-overflow
#    warnings) -- this rules out a binding/generator-layer cause and
#    localizes the bug to play()'s own recovered logic in the region
#    PROMOTIONS.md batch 12 could not verify offline (only 502 of 17420
#    bytes were: the "simulation core" / "score-floor-combo-death"
#    regions, main.c ~3681-3969, original VA ~0x4118xx-0x4121xx, are the
#    leading candidates -- not yet narrowed to one line since the tool
#    that would do it (a per-tick digest) is the very thing finding 1
#    above breaks once play is bound). play_itr.txt and newgame.txt show
#    NO mismatch over their own (narrower) observable overlap, but were
#    not verified to their own score/final-outcome -- absence of evidence,
#    not evidence of absence. See carrier/NOTES.md / src/icytower/
#    INVIVO.md "In-vivo pass -- play()" for the full repro and
#    src/icytower/*.c is out of this task's edit scope (play.c untouched).
play=src
